{"id": "EUVD-2026-76340", "enisaUuid": "c5115b23-f393-3789-9b56-0067f48d4ba9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/chrome: sensorhub: Bound the EC-reported sensor number\n\nEach EC FIFO event carries an 8-bit sensor number (in->sensor_num).\ncros_ec_sensorhub_ring_handler() validates the FIFO event count, the\nper-read count and the ring bound, but not the sensor number, which\ncros_ec_sensor_ring_process_event() then uses unchecked to index\nsensorhub->batch_state[] - allocated with only sensorhub->sensor_num\nentries. A sensor number of sensor_num or larger is an out-of-bounds\nread and write of batch_state[].\n\nValidate the sensor number in the ring handler, where each event is read\nfrom the EC, and drop a malformed event before it is used.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:42", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a76b87e1d065183e2e7ae5b800cb1f6e84f543d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b602ecf6193ecb9720c78b6728d7e09370b1ff1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/324880f94ba3c6269a607e04f78a4dd4a66b3f53", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1b4add68dabfdd6481a4fa198bf3b473d2634d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d2636dce0a8fe9eecad29010699847be425dc80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5eaf7faa99578ae090030d1e2e6ea3b37a615496", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d9bf63ed74f859c6698bc01d8fb216ef9253867", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/833740a2333c2e4db4e02e3d0ffba04e8718a5f3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9fvp-phgh-6gx2", "CVE-2026-81017"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01b178bf-8f6d-3f6d-b023-2da9d88b951b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "0ab90ca4-2e13-3c40-947e-9163a1454960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_